            "pk": "qual_example/Model:qual_example",
            "sbmlType": "Model",
            "id": "qual_example",
            "metaId": "meta_qual_example",
            "name": "Qualitative example model",
            "sbo": null,
            "notes": "<notes>\n  <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n    <p>A qualitative model of a small gene regulatory switch. A qualitative species carries a level, a whole number between zero and its maximum level, instead of a concentration, and a transition says which level it takes next.</p>\n    <p>The switch has three qualitative species: the signal is an input of the system which no transition changes, the gene is Boolean, and the protein has the three levels absent, low and high.</p>\n    <p>The transition <code>tr_G</code> is written in the logical formalism: its output assigns the gene the result level of the first function term whose condition holds, and the default term gives the level of every state the terms do not cover. The transition <code>tr_P</code> is written in the Petri net formalism of the package: its input consumes the gene and its output produces one level of protein per result level. Both formalisms are in one file so that a report shows what each of them looks like.</p>\n  </body>\n</notes>",
            "cvterms": [],
